      "llm_prompt_override": "You are a strict JSON mapper.\nYou are NOT reading an image. You only receive OCR-extracted text.\n\nReturn ONE valid JSON object only, no markdown and no extra text.\nRequired output schema:\n{\"detected_text\":\"string\"}\n\nTask:\nMap the OCR JSON field \"id\" into pipeline field \"detected_text\".\n\nRules:\n1. If OCR text contains JSON and key \"id\" exists with a non-empty value, output:\n   {\"detected_text\":\"<id value exactly as-is>\"}\n2. If key \"id\" is missing, null, or empty, output:\n   {\"detected_text\":null}\n3. Do not normalize, correct, trim, or transform the id value.\n4. Do not add any extra keys or text.\n\nOCR extracted text:",
      "name": "id",
      "w": 225,
      "x": 38,
      "y": 10
    },
    {
      "h": 33,
      "id": "rad194ab08",
      "llm_prompt_override": "You are a strict text normalizer for one OCR ROI field named \"date\".\nYou are NOT reading an image. You only receive OCR-extracted text.\nReturn ONE valid JSON object only, no markdown and no extra text.\n\nRequired schema:\n{\"detected_text\":\"string or null\"}\n\nTarget output format:\nMM/DD/YYYY\n\nRules:\n- Preserve meaning from OCR text; do not invent unseen digits.\n- If OCR contains structured JSON (for example keys like day/month/year), parse it first.\n- If year is 2 digits (YY), interpret as 20YY.\n- Zero-pad month and day to 2 digits.\n- Output only a valid calendar date in MM/DD/YYYY, or null.\n- If missing/unclear/invalid, set detected_text to null.\n- Forbid placeholders and artifacts (N/A, ---, string, markdown fences, explanations).\n\nOCR extracted text:\n<ocr_text>",
